{
    "background_story": "Egghead, a brilliant and eccentric astronomer, spent his entire career studying the mysteries of the universe. His life's work was dedicated to understanding the subtle dance of celestial bodies, particularly the phenomenon of precession. He spent countless nights at the observatory, pouring over ancient texts and modern data, searching for patterns and clues. Egghead's obsession with precession led him to make a groundbreaking discovery: a previously unknown planet whose axis wobbled in a unique pattern, affecting the precession of nearby stars. His findings sent shockwaves through the scientific community, earning him the nickname 'The Precession Prophet.' Egghead's work not only expanded humanity's understanding of the cosmos but also inspired a new generation of astronomers to explore the vast expanse of the universe.",
